WEBVTT

00:00.890 --> 00:03.120
We're almost at Mt. Mud Boat.

00:03.940 --> 00:06.420
By the way, why are we here again?

00:06.420 --> 00:07.950
Um...

00:07.950 --> 00:11.620
This place always has
a lot of UFO sightings,

00:11.620 --> 00:15.840
and most of them seem to happen
around the same time on New Year's Eve.

00:15.840 --> 00:20.500
And this phenomenon apparently
occurs every seven years.

00:20.500 --> 00:23.820
The last time there was a
sighting was seven years ago.

00:23.820 --> 00:25.490
At least, that's what this article said.

00:26.160 --> 00:29.030
Well, all this information
is rather convenient.

00:32.620 --> 00:35.830
You've got this, Mob. We're almost there,
so don't go puking on me.

00:37.080 --> 00:39.540
This road sure is something.

00:39.540 --> 00:42.440
There's supposed to be a
hiking trail somewhere.

00:42.440 --> 00:43.310
Huh?

00:43.310 --> 00:44.460
What's wrong?

00:44.460 --> 00:48.650
I think we passed the sign for
the hiking trail a ways back...

00:48.650 --> 00:51.700
Uh, why didn't you mention that earlier?

00:51.880 --> 00:54.555
I just thought he was trying to take us
(Licensed driver with little experience: 10 years)

00:54.557 --> 00:56.290
as far as he could with the car.
(Licensed driver with little experience: 10 years)

00:56.290 --> 00:57.030
Ugh!
(Licensed driver with little experience: 10 years)

00:57.600 --> 01:02.410
We're gonna have to go in reverse until
we find enough space to make a U-turn.

01:02.940 --> 01:06.650
It's only 1:30 PM, so there's
probably no reason to hurry.

01:06.650 --> 01:10.110
Yeah, says the guy who was an hour late.

01:11.040 --> 01:13.280
Hey, let's calm down.

01:13.280 --> 01:15.610
The UFO's not gonna come
if we're too angry.

01:15.610 --> 01:16.250
Huh?

01:16.520 --> 01:18.490
Are you mocking me?

01:18.490 --> 01:21.480
And after I canceled my plans
for New Year's Eve to be here.

01:21.480 --> 01:22.920
The hell'd you just say?

01:22.920 --> 01:24.680
You were being all pouty,

01:24.680 --> 01:26.983
so we were trying to be nice

01:26.985 --> 01:28.430
The hell's with that attitude?

01:28.430 --> 01:30.020
N-Now, now...

01:35.090 --> 01:38.220
Okay, time to put this baby in reverse.

01:39.020 --> 01:40.500
M-Mob!

01:47.355 --> 01:49.065
(MOB MOB WOW!)

01:50.185 --> 01:51.935
(MOB MOB WOW!)

01:53.105 --> 01:54.775
(MOB MOB WOW!)

01:55.945 --> 01:57.615
(MOB MOB WOW!)

01:59.025 --> 02:01.745
I realized that our youth is gray

02:01.745 --> 02:04.665
The origin of this uneasiness
Is yet unknown

02:04.745 --> 02:07.165
Trains of emotions keep running
Through my brain

02:07.165 --> 02:10.335
Struggling through this adolescence

02:10.455 --> 02:13.295
Don't disturb my deep psyche

02:13.295 --> 02:15.965
Who is that behind you?

02:16.085 --> 02:19.755
Opposing ideas creates distortion

02:19.755 --> 02:23.175
Exorcise all the sorrow

02:23.345 --> 02:26.845
So, do what you can now

02:26.935 --> 02:28.765
My life

02:29.015 --> 02:32.895
Finally, break it down

02:34.395 --> 02:37.235
(Want) Both greed
(Young) And honesty

02:37.235 --> 02:40.115
(Burn) Are growing
(1) On this chest of mine

02:40.115 --> 02:42.865
(Trance) I'm not waking up
(Chance) I want to wake up

02:42.865 --> 02:45.825
(Stance) These two different faces of mine
(1) Are standing back-to-back

02:45.825 --> 02:48.325
Taking things as it is

02:48.325 --> 02:51.745
In this free relation where
We resent each other

02:51.835 --> 02:54.045
Once these two become one

02:54.045 --> 02:56.045
That smile becomes one

02:56.045 --> 02:59.135
And only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

02:59.795 --> 03:02.805
"1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:03.135 --> 03:04.215
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:04.215 --> 03:07.095
One and only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:07.265 --> 03:08.805
"1"

03:08.805 --> 03:09.975
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:09.975 --> 03:12.265
One and only "1"

03:13.960 --> 03:18.460
(Communicating 2
~Encountering the Unknown~)

03:23.810 --> 03:25.430
Are you okay?

03:25.960 --> 03:27.740
Thank goodness. There's reception.

03:28.178 --> 03:32.168
All right. Let's walk back
towards the hiking trail.

03:32.170 --> 03:35.370
I'll come back to get the car later.

03:36.660 --> 03:39.760
If we're going to walk, why don't we keep
going forward rather than go back?

03:39.760 --> 03:41.290
Yeah, not happening.

03:41.290 --> 03:44.620
Amateurs shouldn't walk the game trails
of mountains they're not familiar with.

03:44.820 --> 03:47.830
I won't be able to take any responsibility
if something happens to you kids.

03:48.310 --> 03:52.340
Um... Sorry, I'm gonna go take a piss.

03:53.070 --> 03:54.920
Mob, you should go, too.

03:57.980 --> 03:59.690
They don't seem to be coming back.

04:00.850 --> 04:03.010
They aren't going number two, are they?

04:03.010 --> 04:05.900
Did they get lost? I'll go take a look.

04:05.900 --> 04:08.900
Hold it. It's dangerous to go alone.
We'll all go together.

04:09.110 --> 04:10.080
That way?

04:10.080 --> 04:11.340
No, it's that way.

04:22.020 --> 04:24.160
Which way did we come from again?

04:24.940 --> 04:28.300
We've definitely lost the path.

04:28.830 --> 04:30.700
And now there's no reception.

04:31.570 --> 04:34.110
Uh, we're probably gonna be
in trouble if it gets dark.

04:34.110 --> 04:36.410
Sh-Should we head back down?

04:36.410 --> 04:38.770
Whenever you get lost in the mountains...

04:38.770 --> 04:44.630
I've heard that it's probably safer to
head up the mountain than try to go back down.

04:45.180 --> 04:47.360
If we can get to a better vantage point,

04:47.360 --> 04:49.190
we should be able to find a route.

04:49.510 --> 04:50.860
Oh, I see.

04:50.860 --> 04:54.480
I should've placed more obvious
markers along the way...

04:54.680 --> 04:57.920
He sure seems knowledgeable,
even if he's an amateur.

04:58.700 --> 05:01.650
Oh, crap! I left the book back in the car.

05:01.650 --> 05:02.440
What? You're kidding.

05:02.700 --> 05:06.270
The one that has the spell for
the UFO summoning ritual?!

05:08.700 --> 05:10.310
It's no big deal.

05:17.720 --> 05:19.490
Look, it's the mountain trail.

05:19.830 --> 05:22.900
I think we might just make
it if we keep going!

05:22.900 --> 05:25.470
Huh? Weren't we heading back?

05:26.810 --> 05:30.460
We've come this far,
so let's actually summon a UFO!

05:30.770 --> 05:35.010
Yeah, that's not happening. We've been
messing up left and right all day.

05:35.270 --> 05:37.010
Seriously, Kurata...

05:37.010 --> 05:41.850
Who do you think Inukawa and Saruta
painstakingly planned this all out for?

05:41.850 --> 05:43.970
What? Really?

05:44.720 --> 05:47.800
Are you seriously trying to
blame this on me right now?

05:48.210 --> 05:53.200
I disbanded the Brainwave Club because
all of you never tried to do anything!

05:53.590 --> 05:55.430
Today's no different.

05:55.430 --> 05:57.700
I kept wondering if I should come or not!

05:58.600 --> 06:00.820
Because I didn't want this
very thing to happen.

06:01.330 --> 06:05.670
I only came because I believed you
when you said you found a telepathist.

06:06.090 --> 06:09.340
And yet you had the nerve to lie to me...

06:09.750 --> 06:15.590
None of you have any idea how I feel
getting my earnest hopes trampled on.

06:18.050 --> 06:19.070
How could you?!

06:19.510 --> 06:21.430
How could you?!

06:23.780 --> 06:26.770
Anyway, there's really no point
in arguing right now,

06:26.770 --> 06:28.510
so why don't we keep on walking?

06:28.510 --> 06:31.020
No, I'm going home! I'm leaving!

06:31.670 --> 06:34.850
I'm tired! I'm not climbing any farther!

06:35.510 --> 06:39.030
I'll go back alone,
so all of you can keep on going.

06:40.510 --> 06:41.670
Tome-san.

06:41.670 --> 06:43.010
Let's walk together.

06:49.800 --> 06:53.480
Okay, fine. I just need
to keep walking, right?

06:54.860 --> 06:56.400
All right, let's go.

07:12.330 --> 07:14.720
Man, we're high up.

07:14.720 --> 07:15.640
We did it.

07:15.640 --> 07:18.050
4:19 PM...

07:18.050 --> 07:21.090
We don't have much time before
the sun's gonna set.

07:21.090 --> 07:27.060
Well... According to the documents,
the UFO usually appears around 5 PM,

07:27.060 --> 07:29.190
so let's get ready to summon it.

07:31.390 --> 07:35.270
Are we really doing this?
Didn't you forget the book in the car?

07:35.950 --> 07:39.430
Prez, you were always reading that book.

07:39.430 --> 07:43.790
You don't have the spell to
summon aliens memorized?

07:44.490 --> 07:47.190
Of course I don't.

07:47.930 --> 07:51.980
Isn't it enough that we all climbed
to the top of the mountain together?

07:51.980 --> 07:54.450
We've already made plenty
of memories today.

07:54.960 --> 07:56.400
This is a great view.

07:58.870 --> 08:00.980
What are you doing, Takenaka?

08:04.690 --> 08:05.740
Ahem...

08:07.940 --> 08:10.860
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari...

08:11.260 --> 08:14.150
Prooha komo hipakaeeh...

08:16.610 --> 08:21.060
After creating an 8 with the rocks and
setting a foot in either circle,

08:21.060 --> 08:24.440
close your eyes and chant while facing
in the southwest direction...

08:24.740 --> 08:26.390
Hands should look like this.

08:26.860 --> 08:29.030
I know you remember this, Prez.

08:30.550 --> 08:36.470
I got pretty serious researching all of this
and before I knew it, it was morning.

08:36.470 --> 08:40.980
So... you weren't late because you
overslept from being too nervous?

08:41.420 --> 08:44.050
This is way too embarrassing to even say.

08:44.050 --> 08:48.660
The last thing I wanted to do was mess it
up, so I figured I'd do whatever I could.

08:48.940 --> 08:51.330
You were that serious about this?

08:51.670 --> 08:53.080
Yeah, I am.

08:53.080 --> 08:57.100
I decided I'd help out because these
three were so serious about all this.

08:57.540 --> 08:59.880
So could you believe us already?

09:01.050 --> 09:02.060
But...

09:02.580 --> 09:05.310
"Even then, I'm scared of
this going wrong.

09:06.070 --> 09:10.400
It's probably better to limit this
to chasing a fantasy.

09:11.400 --> 09:15.230
Maybe all that matters in this
is whether we had fun.

09:15.750 --> 09:20.650
Because my other memories with
everyone may all end up a joke, too.

09:21.420 --> 09:25.220
We almost got lost in the mountains
because I'm forcing my delusions on them.

09:26.160 --> 09:30.620
I don't want to face reality
any more than this..." Apparently.

09:30.620 --> 09:34.910
No way! We don't think you're
forcing your delusions on us.

09:34.910 --> 09:37.440
This is something we wanted to do!

09:37.440 --> 09:39.760
Before the Brainwave Club disbands.

09:41.120 --> 09:42.570
Boys...

09:43.530 --> 09:44.480
Then...

09:44.480 --> 09:46.910
Then you should've just said so earlier!

09:47.230 --> 09:49.110
Would it kill her to be honest?

09:49.110 --> 09:51.480
If that's the case, we're all doing this.

09:51.480 --> 09:53.750
Come on, start lining up those rocks.

09:54.330 --> 09:57.110
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari...

09:57.110 --> 09:59.790
Prooha komo hipakaeeh...

09:59.790 --> 10:02.580
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari...

10:02.810 --> 10:03.930
Master?

10:04.580 --> 10:07.870
You said you researched this
all last night, right?

10:07.870 --> 10:10.690
Are you sure you didn't
find out anything else?

10:10.690 --> 10:13.500
Huh? Is your master a telepathist, too?

10:13.760 --> 10:16.780
No, I am not a telepathist...

10:16.780 --> 10:20.460
but I can read minds by observing
the subtle changes in your aura.

10:21.310 --> 10:23.350
Apparently, he's the kind
of guy that's a total liar

10:23.350 --> 10:26.090
but is good at reading people through
their actions and mannerisms.

10:26.400 --> 10:30.550
Well, Takenaka?
Are you hiding anything else?

10:31.750 --> 10:36.730
Well, the author of that occult book
was arrested two years ago for fraud.

10:37.480 --> 10:41.690
The research in that book has no basis.

10:41.690 --> 10:43.680
Even this ritual is completely fake.

10:43.680 --> 10:45.010
Seriously?

10:45.370 --> 10:47.630
So you're saying this is pointless?

10:47.630 --> 10:48.840
What the hell?

10:49.250 --> 10:52.040
I-I'm sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

10:52.040 --> 10:56.540
I figured there was purpose in the
Brainwave Club working together, though.

10:56.830 --> 10:58.610
And you're exactly right.

10:58.610 --> 11:01.280
It's always worth it to do your best.

11:01.280 --> 11:04.640
All of you ended up gathering
information and took action.

11:04.640 --> 11:06.340
That's pretty impressive.

11:06.340 --> 11:11.220
I'm sure this whole thing will always
be a precious memory of your youth.

11:11.510 --> 11:15.680
It will always remain an important
experience in your hearts.

11:16.310 --> 11:18.510
And you should be proud of that.

11:19.110 --> 11:22.590
Y-You're right. We all did our best.

11:22.590 --> 11:24.080
Y-Yeah.

11:24.080 --> 11:26.080
There's no denying that we
actually did work hard.

11:26.080 --> 11:27.120
I guess...

11:27.120 --> 11:30.400
All right. It's getting pretty
dark, so let's head back.

11:31.080 --> 11:35.460
What about the UFO sightings?
Were those also fake?

11:35.460 --> 11:37.910
No, apparently those really happened.

11:38.290 --> 11:39.450
I see.

11:46.180 --> 11:47.240
Then, let's do it.

11:47.240 --> 11:49.220
We haven't tried everything yet.

11:51.840 --> 11:53.630
Let's send out a telepathic message.

11:53.630 --> 11:56.860
I'll give it my all, too,
so let's all try again.

11:57.420 --> 11:58.600
Mob-kun...

11:59.200 --> 12:01.420
Prez, do you want to try it?

12:01.420 --> 12:02.440
Let's do it.

12:02.440 --> 12:03.190
Yeah.

12:03.190 --> 12:04.410
Come on, President Kurata.

12:04.920 --> 12:07.860
Boys... Thank you.

12:35.830 --> 12:37.480
Don't try moving too much.

12:38.160 --> 12:39.790
Did you try too hard?

12:40.280 --> 12:43.460
I-I'll be okay. But...

12:44.080 --> 12:46.310
Dang it... I guess it didn't work.

12:53.250 --> 12:56.330
Why all the long faces?

12:56.330 --> 12:57.960
I-I mean...

12:58.220 --> 13:02.090
Psychics and telepathists actually exist.

13:02.660 --> 13:05.860
I'm sure we'll be able to
communicate with aliens someday!

13:06.420 --> 13:11.090
Just look at
how many stars are in the sky!

13:11.930 --> 13:13.480
There's no reason to hurry.

13:13.970 --> 13:17.260
I'm having plenty of fun being
with all of you, so it's fine.

13:20.040 --> 13:20.730
Huh?

13:29.030 --> 13:30.990
(Line up the rocks and
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari!!)

13:32.040 --> 13:34.500
(An Unidentified Flying Object
Actually Existed!)

13:35.350 --> 13:36.960
Is this for real?

13:36.960 --> 13:38.390
It actually came?

13:38.770 --> 13:42.500
Wai...Wh-Wh-What do we do?!
What am I supposed to do?!

13:42.500 --> 13:46.200
Y-You're the one who wanted
to meet the aliens, Prez!

13:46.200 --> 13:48.010
Y-Y-Yeah, b-but...

13:49.320 --> 13:50.540
- Prez! Behind you! Behind you!

13:50.540 --> 13:52.350
- S-Something's coming!
- Prez! Behind you! Behind you!

13:52.350 --> 13:53.840
That was quick!

13:53.840 --> 13:57.420
Uh, I... D-D-Do we have anything?!
Like a bug-catching net?

13:57.420 --> 13:59.330
Why are you thinking about
capturing them?!

13:59.330 --> 14:01.890
Who knows what'll happen
if we make them mad?!

14:07.610 --> 14:11.080
Th-This is what aliens look like?

14:11.400 --> 14:13.040
Thin limbs...

14:13.040 --> 14:16.790
Giant, developed heads...
Super-smooth skin...

14:17.370 --> 14:20.210
Humongous, sparkly eyes...

14:20.210 --> 14:23.170
There's no doubt about it.
They're the real deal!

14:23.740 --> 14:27.140
They really do seem otherworldly...

14:27.140 --> 14:29.160
I wonder if we can communicate with them.

14:29.160 --> 14:31.420
They have really pretty eyes, though.

14:32.410 --> 14:34.200
I don't sense any malice.

14:34.200 --> 14:36.410
It seems like they want to shake hands...

14:36.410 --> 14:37.910
Wait, with me?

14:37.910 --> 14:39.850
I-I'd be honored!

14:39.850 --> 14:42.850
I can't believe I get to greet them on
behalf of Earth before anyone else!

14:43.160 --> 14:44.440
Hey, I really wouldn't!

14:44.440 --> 14:47.040
You never know what kind of
germs they're carrying.

14:47.500 --> 14:48.650
Master...

14:57.530 --> 15:00.040
Good for you, President Kurata.

15:07.050 --> 15:09.990
Apparently, they want to show us
the inside of their spacecraft.

15:09.990 --> 15:10.950
Really?!

15:10.950 --> 15:12.830
Sweet! That's awesome!

15:12.830 --> 15:14.380
Let's go, everyone!

15:16.970 --> 15:19.730
A-Are you sure it's okay to get on?

15:20.620 --> 15:22.010
I'll go, too.

15:25.610 --> 15:28.490
In for a penny, in for a pound, I guess...

15:51.530 --> 15:54.200
This really reminds me of our club room.

15:58.910 --> 16:01.980
They're, like, super friendly.

16:02.400 --> 16:05.520
I sorta figured they'd be kinda scary.

16:06.920 --> 16:11.340
Prez, it's always been your dream to
interact with extraterrestrial lifeforms, right?

16:11.340 --> 16:14.730
This is your chance to ask them all kinds of
things with Takenaka as your interpreter!

16:15.040 --> 16:17.510
Yeah, I think I can make it work.

16:18.830 --> 16:24.040
R-Right... Um... Uh...

16:31.340 --> 16:33.100
I can't think of anything.

16:34.370 --> 16:37.550
Oh, I know.
Why don't we play some games?

16:37.550 --> 16:39.810
I always have this thing on me.

16:42.890 --> 16:46.150
Nice! Let's show them how it works!

17:22.570 --> 17:24.690
It's a new year...

17:25.760 --> 17:29.950
All this is going on, yet all I can think
about is the turn of the year

17:29.950 --> 17:32.650
and the late fees for the rental car...

17:33.590 --> 17:35.780
They're blinding...

17:39.200 --> 17:42.830
Whoa, it's almost morning.
We should head home soon.

17:43.450 --> 17:44.730
You're right.

17:44.730 --> 17:48.640
I, at least, told my parents I was spending
the night at a friend's house, but...

17:48.640 --> 17:51.800
I mean, I guess we're all
friends now anyway.

17:54.750 --> 17:57.730
All right, let's start wrapping things up.

18:05.450 --> 18:07.290
I wonder if it's a gift.

18:07.770 --> 18:09.150
It's so pretty.

18:10.250 --> 18:13.350
It's a token of their friendship,
apparently.

18:17.100 --> 18:18.760
They just keep staring.

18:18.760 --> 18:21.540
Maybe we should give them
something in return?

18:22.090 --> 18:25.660
Then, I'll give them my scarf.

18:28.850 --> 18:32.450
Um... Then I'll give them this notebook.

18:32.880 --> 18:35.180
Here's my watch...
It's pretty cheap, but...

18:35.380 --> 18:37.130
You can have my gum.

18:37.130 --> 18:39.100
Here's this gaming console from Earth.

18:39.420 --> 18:42.140
Hm... I don't have anything.

18:42.570 --> 18:45.810
Maybe I can show them some of my powers.

18:47.680 --> 18:49.630
They seem pretty happy with that.

18:49.630 --> 18:51.590
Oh, that's good.

18:54.060 --> 18:56.730
Uh... Why are you stripping, Reigen-san?

18:57.090 --> 19:00.630
I was in a hurry this morning, so I'm
still wearing my pajamas underneath.

19:02.290 --> 19:03.380
You can have this.

19:04.100 --> 19:05.460
They're very happy.

19:05.460 --> 19:06.910
I guess anything goes.

19:14.230 --> 19:16.350
Thank you so much for coming to see us.

19:21.570 --> 19:25.760
Well, we'll be on our way now.
Let's meet again someday!

19:40.580 --> 19:42.520
Hey, the first sunrise of the year.

19:44.120 --> 19:47.100
I'll never forget today.

19:47.580 --> 19:51.310
I'm sure everyone else feels
the same... I just know it.

19:54.350 --> 19:55.540
Hey, wait.

19:56.620 --> 19:57.850
Where's Inukawa?

20:09.060 --> 20:10.540
New Year's Eve.

20:11.190 --> 20:13.680
I was taken away by a UFO.

20:18.580 --> 20:24.540
I'm going to try to convince them
to take me back to Earth.

20:25.710 --> 20:28.100
But I'm dealing with aliens.

20:29.420 --> 20:31.630
I can't communicate with them.

20:31.630 --> 20:34.220
This is probably going to be
a long, drawn-out battle.

20:35.260 --> 20:38.570
For now, I think I'm going to keep writing
down my progress in this notebook.

20:42.270 --> 20:48.550
The next day, they all threw me a
welcome party...? Or something.

20:48.940 --> 20:53.320
I had no idea what any of this stuff is,
but in the end, I chose something and ate it.

20:54.170 --> 20:57.060
After that,
my memories are a little foggy,

20:57.060 --> 21:01.560
but I think something insane happened.

21:07.150 --> 21:13.090
When I came to, I was in another unfamiliar
place, and my head was killing me.

21:14.620 --> 21:20.710
That day, I realized just how much a
little bit of gaming time would mean to me.

21:21.530 --> 21:23.580
But, more importantly,
I wanted to go home.

21:27.630 --> 21:30.610
The inhabitants of this planet
have a natural enemy.

21:30.610 --> 21:34.800
It's a savage monster that
tries to eat all of their crops.

21:37.640 --> 21:39.860
Despite being such an advanced race,

21:39.860 --> 21:44.210
they'd never thought of using weapons.

21:49.600 --> 21:52.210
And so, I took care of that pest for them.

21:53.430 --> 21:56.590
It ended up being about the size
of the dog I have back home.

22:07.600 --> 22:11.800
It might be because I slew their monster,
but they treated me like a hero,

22:11.800 --> 22:16.940
so life on this planet
isn't so bad after all.

22:21.120 --> 22:25.280
I have no idea how much
time has passed now.

22:31.070 --> 22:32.360
Everyone!

22:33.290 --> 22:35.360
I have something I need to tell you!

22:41.950 --> 22:48.150
On the brink of loneliness, Inukawa was
able to link his thoughts with the aliens

22:48.150 --> 22:52.170
and tell them that he wanted
to go back home to Earth.

23:01.810 --> 23:06.750
If you have something you want to say,
just look them in the eyes,

23:06.750 --> 23:08.850
and you'll be able to get through to them.

23:09.530 --> 23:14.160
Inukawa realized this,
but by the time he got back to Earth,

23:14.160 --> 23:18.770
most of his memories had
become fuzzy and vague.

23:26.300 --> 23:27.240
What?

23:27.240 --> 23:28.220
You're joking, right?

23:28.900 --> 23:29.460
What?

23:29.970 --> 23:31.160
Really?

23:31.790 --> 23:33.880
Tsubomi-chan is... transferring?

23:34.790 --> 23:37.640
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 III Episode 9:

23:37.640 --> 23:37.650
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 III Episode 9:

23:37.650 --> 23:40.010
"Mob 1 ~Moving~"
